		<div class="topic" id="forum_op_topic_568175240219519653">
		People will be blown away in a year or two, when big AI projects will begin to release.	</div>
	<div class="content" id="forum_op_content_568175240219519653">
		Blown like never before. You will have so many games to choose from, and so cheap, that you'll wet your pants. The gaming industry will be flipped on its head. You will have 1000 more games than now in a few years. And there will be super unique and original stuff there also.	</div>
		
	<div class="forum_op_footer">
		<div class="forum_audit">
			Last edited by <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198049654196" class="hoverunderline">diesoon</a>;
		<span  title="October 26, 2026 @ 9:39:30 pm PDT" data-timestamp="1793075970">Oct 26 @ 9:39pm</span>		</div>
			</div>
</div>
<div data-featuretarget="community-awards"></div>
<script type="text/javascript">
	$J( function() {
		InitializeForumTopic( {"owner":"46329996","type":"General","feature":"0","gidforum":"582809103434380736","forum_display_name":"General Discussions","forum_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5186030\/discussions\/0\/","forum_search_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5186030\/discussions\/search\/","is_public":1,"permissions":{"can_view":1,"can_post":1,"can_reply":1,"is_banned":0,"can_delete":0,"can_edit":0},"appid":5186030}, "https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/forum\/46329996\/General\/",
		"568175240219519653", {"author":"diesoon","text":"Blown like never before. You will have so many games to choose from, and so cheap, that you'll wet your pants. The gaming industry will be flipped on its head. You will have 1000 more games than now in a few years. And there will be super unique and original stuff there also."}		);
			} );
</script>
										<script type="text/javascript">
$J( function() { InitializeCommentThread( "ForumTopic", "ForumTopic_103582791475851404_582809103434380736_568175240219519653", {"feature":"582809103434380736","feature2":"568175240219519653","owner":"103582791475851404","commentthreadid":"661284016","total_count":12,"start":0,"pagesize":15,"has_upvoted":0,"upvotes":0,"votecountid":null,"voteupid":null,"commentcountid":null,"subscribed":false,"extended_data":"{\"topic_permissions\":{\"can_view\":1,\"can_post\":1,\"can_reply\":1,\"is_banned\":0,\"can_delete\":0,\"can_edit\":0},\"original_poster\":89388468,\"topic_gidanswer\":\"0\",\"forum_appid\":5186030,\"forum_public\":1,\"forum_type\":\"General\",\"forum_gidfeature\":\"0\"}","oldestfirst":true,"comments_raw":{"568175240219530394":{"text":"Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality.\n\nAI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff.","author":"Scyrenus"},"568175523960728551":{"text":"[quote=Scyrenus;568175240219530394]Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality.\n\nAI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. [\/quote]\nThe neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient.","author":"\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622"},"568175523960728650":{"text":"[quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;568175523960728551][quote=Scyrenus;568175240219530394]Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality.\n\nAI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. [\/quote]\nThe neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. [\/quote]\nSure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole.","author":"Scyrenus"},"568175523960729316":{"text":"[quote=Scyrenus;568175523960728650][quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;568175523960728551]\nThe neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. [\/quote]\nSure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. [\/quote]\nPeople said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money.","author":"\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622"},"568175523960729757":{"text":"[quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;568175523960729316][quote=Scyrenus;568175523960728650]\nSure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. [\/quote]\nPeople said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money. [\/quote]\nSure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning.","author":"Scyrenus"},"568175523960745317":{"text":"People rejected radio, TV, the Internet and now AI. They'll come to learn to accept it, or be left behind. Either way, AI [b]IS[\/b] the future.","author":"Poyzo"},"568175523960767172":{"text":"[quote=Scyrenus;568175240219530394]Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality.\n\nAI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. [\/quote]\nYou will just abandon your backlog again because new mindblowing stuff made with AI will arrive, and you won't care, you will just enjoy.","author":"diesoon"},"568175523960777299":{"text":"[quote=diesoon;568175523960767172][quote=Scyrenus;568175240219530394]Doubt. Before the AI-prompt era, I already had a library of games that I would never finish in my lifetime because of the obvious human mortality.\n\nAI will help me slow down on purchases and focus on the old stuff. [\/quote]\nYou will just abandon your backlog again because new mindblowing stuff made with AI will arrive, and you won't care, you will just enjoy. [\/quote]\nKnowing my snobby ahh, I absolutely doubt it. After all I do keep playing old games over and over again even now. + I will always care, I love watching and studying behind the scenes to see how stuff is made.","author":"Scyrenus"},"569301473354076552":{"text":"[quote=Scyrenus;568175523960729757][quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;568175523960729316]\nPeople said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money. [\/quote]\nSure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. [\/quote]\nJust because something takes a lot of time or effort to produce doesn't mean it will appeal to people, like carving figurines out of wood requires considerable time and effort, but it's not like there are a lot of people who would actually want to buy these wooden figurines. Most people would rather buy a mass-produced figurine molded by a machine in a factory. AI is just another tool exactly like the camera, that enables people to create their own envisioned games. If the end product is good then it doesn't matter if AI was involved or not.","author":"\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622"},"569301473354084812":{"text":"[quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;569301473354076552][quote=Scyrenus;568175523960729757]\nSure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. [\/quote]\nJust because something takes a lot of time or effort to produce doesn't mean it will appeal to people, like carving figurines out of wood requires considerable time and effort, but it's not like there are a lot of people who would actually want to buy these wooden figurines. Most people would rather buy a mass-produced figurine molded by a machine in a factory. AI is just another tool exactly like the camera, that enables people to create their own envisioned games. If the end product is good then it doesn't matter if AI was involved or not. [\/quote]\nAyyy, thanks, now I want to visit some artsy craftsy stores to start making figurines.\n\nAlso, we're not talking about appeal here, people have always loved cheap slop even during pre-AI era.\n\nAnd I do agree that effort doesn't always pay off, but it does teach you a lot even if it is a failed endeavor. If it is made by AI the final product is only a product, it inherently cannot be considered good or bad, it simply exists with no value attached to it. Because why would I pay for something if the developers didn't bother putting a part of themselves into the project?","author":"Scyrenus"},"569301473354233822":{"text":"Thats something that a person who is depending on AI to succeed would say. You are not fooling me AI Simp! AI WILL NOT REPLACES US!","author":"REDSHADOW"},"569301473354357614":{"text":"[quote=Scyrenus;568175523960729757][quote=\u2622Paradoxic Gamer\u2622;568175523960729316]\nPeople said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money. [\/quote]\nSure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. [\/quote]\n\n\nWhat are you talking about? Taking a photo is just point and shoot. You just press a button. \ud83d\ude01","author":"Super Jelly"}},"track_navigation":true}, 'https://steamcommunity.com/comment/ForumTopic/', 40 ); } );
</script>
