			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_568175523960729316">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568175523960728650">Scyrenus</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568175523960728551">☢Paradoxic Gamer☢</a></b>:</div>The neoluddite attitude will fade with time, newer generations will embrace the future which is AI, same thing happened with horse drawn carriages, they were eventually replaced by the combustion engine. Not using AI is vastly ineffecient. </blockquote>Sure, using AI as a tool is great to check grammar, reorganize spreadsheets, and to help with science, but keep it away from art with a thousand-mile-long pole. </blockquote>People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money.			</div>
