						<div data-panel="{&quot;flow-children&quot;:&quot;row&quot;}" class="community_award_ctn" id="community_awards_comment_569301473354076552"></div>
					</div>
					<div class="commentthread_comment_timestamp">
											</div>
					<div class="commentthread_comment_timestamp" title="October 27, 2026 @ 7:15:29 pm PDT" data-timestamp="1793153729">
						Oct 27 @ 7:15pm&nbsp;
					</div>
				</div>

				
				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_569301473354076552">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_569301473354076552">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475851404', '582809103434380736', '568175240219519653', '82010053', '569301473354076552' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_569301473354076552">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568175523960729757">Scyrenus</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c568175523960729316">☢Paradoxic Gamer☢</a></b>:</div>People said the same about digital art or the camera. AI is just another amazing tool. And video games are more than just art, they are entertainment, if AI vastly reduces the cost of producing video games, that means we will get vastly more content rich video games with higher quality graphics and animations. Your comment would have had some validity if artists weren't restricted by time and money. </blockquote>Sure, but it still takes skill, effort, and intent to create good photos using a camera or to create digital art. If all you care about is more content, then it is fine. Heck, I even play idle games to get that serotonin running in my brain from time to time, but in general I care more about how things are made and what the artist is trying to convey. Otherwise, content for the sake of content is simply bland, degrading slop. There is a reason why some newer artists are returning to older methods of mediums in music, movies, and video games, because people still crave that old authenticity that gives art meaning. </blockquote>Just because something takes a lot of time or effort to produce doesn't mean it will appeal to people, like carving figurines out of wood requires considerable time and effort, but it's not like there are a lot of people who would actually want to buy these wooden figurines. Most people would rather buy a mass-produced figurine molded by a machine in a factory. AI is just another tool exactly like the camera, that enables people to create their own envisioned games. If the end product is good then it doesn't matter if AI was involved or not.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
									<div class="forum_comment_permlink">
						<span class="forum_comment_moderate">
													</span>
												<a data-panel="{&quot;focusable&quot;:false}" href="#c569301473354076552">#9</a>
											</div>
							</div>
		</div>
	</div>
		
	
